$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514372 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186514240 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514372 #edb/ref 1069 "q-95671" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514372 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514372 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\nFind the derivative of $y=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x-4\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514372 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "16fea3d9-04d8-53ba-a81e-4ab7949c02d8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514372 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we recall the results for the derivatives of the basic hyperbolic functions:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x)=\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x)=\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x)={sech}^{2}⁡x\n$$\n\nDifferentiating the given function using these results, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x-4\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x)-4\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{sech}^{2}⁡x-4\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514396 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186514301 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514396 #edb/ref 1069 "q-95679" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514396 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514396 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\nFind the derivative of $f(x)=\\sqrt{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514396 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "443677a2-c964-52f1-8cf6-218af419b0bb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514396 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we express $f(x)$ as a composite function:\n\n$$\nf=\\sqrt{g},\\,g=\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x\n$$\n\nThe chain rule states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}g}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}g}=\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{g}},\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x.\n$$\n\nFinally, multiplying the two results together and substituting for $g$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{g}}\\cdot \\operatorname{sinh}⁡x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x}}\\cdot \\operatorname{sinh}⁡x \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x}{2\\sqrt{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514398 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186514317 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514398 #edb/ref 1069 "q-165764" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514398 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514398 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\nFind the derivative of $f(x)={e}^{\\operatorname{tanh}⁡{x}^{2}}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514398 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "49c81891-b661-5bda-b31c-54f1cc0220f3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514398 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we express $f(x)$ as a composite function:\n\n$$\nf={e}^{g},\\,g=\\operatorname{tanh}⁡s,\\,s={x}^{2}\n$$\n\nThe chain rule states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}g}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}g}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}s}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}g}={e}^{g},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}s}={sech}^{2}⁡s,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}x}=2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, multiplying the three results together and substituting for $g$ and $s$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{g}\\cdot {sech}^{2}⁡s\\cdot 2x \\\\  & ={e}^{\\operatorname{tanh}⁡{x}^{2}}\\cdot {sech}^{2}⁡{x}^{2}\\cdot 2x \\\\  & =2x{e}^{\\operatorname{tanh}⁡{x}^{2}}{sech}^{2}⁡{x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514406 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186514339 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514406 #edb/ref 1069 "q-165768" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514406 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514406 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\nFind the derivative of $t(x)={x}^{4}\\operatorname{tanh}⁡{x}^{3}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514406 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "5d5258aa-0eff-5685-bbfc-832665398ac8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514406 #edb/ref 1074 "Here, we have the product of two functions $u(x)={x}^{4}$ and $v(x)=\\operatorname{tanh}⁡{x}^{3}.$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{′}(x) & =({x}^{4})^{′}\\cdot \\operatorname{tanh}⁡{x}^{3}+{x}^{4}\\cdot (\\operatorname{tanh}⁡{x}^{3})^{′} \\\\  & =4{x}^{3}\\cdot \\operatorname{tanh}⁡{x}^{3}+{x}^{4}\\cdot 3{x}^{2}{sech}^{2}⁡{x}^{3} \\\\  & =4{x}^{3}\\operatorname{tanh}⁡{x}^{3}+3{x}^{6}{sech}^{2}⁡{x}^{3} \\\\  & ={x}^{3}(4\\operatorname{tanh}⁡{x}^{3}+3{x}^{3}{sech}^{2}⁡{x}^{3})\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514408 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186514233 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514408 #edb/ref 1069 "q-95273" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514408 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514408 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\nFind the derivative of $f(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\operatorname{cosh}⁡{x}^{2}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514408 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "5de32c1d-3413-5361-b37c-92eba300a033" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514408 #edb/ref 1074 "Here, we have the product of two functions $u(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x$ and $v(x)=\\operatorname{cosh}⁡{x}^{2}.$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)^{′}\\cdot \\operatorname{cosh}⁡{x}^{2}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\cdot (\\operatorname{cosh}⁡{x}^{2})^{′} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{x}\\cdot \\operatorname{cosh}⁡{x}^{2}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\cdot 2x\\operatorname{sinh}⁡{x}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡{x}^{2}}{x}+2x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\operatorname{sinh}⁡{x}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{x}(\\operatorname{cosh}⁡{x}^{2}+2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\operatorname{sinh}⁡{x}^{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514410 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186514281 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514410 #edb/ref 1069 "q-95319" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514410 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514410 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\nFind the derivative of $g(x)=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514410 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "620df981-8ac1-59e8-bd3d-58c107521764" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514410 #edb/ref 1074 "In this case, the expression for $g(x)$ is a quotient $\\frac{u(x)}{v(x)}$ with $u(x)={x}^{2}$ and $v(x)=\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x.$ \n\nTherefore, we apply the quotient rule as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{{u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{({x}^{2})^{′}\\cdot \\operatorname{cosh}⁡x-{x}^{2}\\cdot (\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x)^{′}}{(\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2x\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x-{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x}{{cosh}^{2}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{x(2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x-x\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x)}{{cosh}^{2}⁡x}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514429 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186514325 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514429 #edb/ref 1069 "q-95682" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514429 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514429 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\nFind the derivative of $f(x)=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sinh}⁡{x}^{3}}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514429 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "7c706f9d-3f1b-52c2-a133-ccf4032fcc0e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514429 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we express $f(x)$ as a composite function:\n\n$$\nf=\\frac{1}{g},\\,g=\\operatorname{sinh}⁡s,\\,s={x}^{3}\n$$\n\nThe chain rule states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}g}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}g}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}s}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}g} & =-\\frac{1}{{g}^{2}},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}s}=\\operatorname{cosh}⁡s,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}x}=3{x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, multiplying the three results together and substituting for $g$ and $s$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{1}{{g}^{2}}\\cdot \\operatorname{cosh}⁡s\\cdot 3{x}^{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{{sinh}^{2}⁡{x}^{3}}\\cdot \\operatorname{cosh}⁡{x}^{3}\\cdot 3{x}^{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡{x}^{3}}{{sinh}^{2}⁡{x}^{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514436 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186514222 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514436 #edb/ref 1069 "q-95674" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514436 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514436 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\nFind the derivative of $y=\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514436 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "925db400-88a9-5795-a4b0-aad7734a8104" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514436 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we recall the results for the derivatives of the basic hyperbolic functions:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x)=\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x)=\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x)={sech}^{2}⁡x\n$$\n\nDifferentiating the given function using these results, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514447 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186514306 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514447 #edb/ref 1069 "q-165769" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514447 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514447 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\nFind the derivative of $f(x)={e}^{3x}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡{x}^{4}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514447 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a7015904-a594-5558-b15e-195c0d212c67" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514447 #edb/ref 1074 "Here, we have the product of two functions $u(x)={e}^{3x}$ and $v(x)=\\operatorname{sinh}⁡{x}^{4}.$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =({e}^{3x})^{′}\\cdot \\operatorname{sinh}⁡{x}^{4}+{e}^{3x}\\cdot (\\operatorname{sinh}⁡{x}^{4})^{′} \\\\  & =3{e}^{3x}\\cdot \\operatorname{sinh}⁡{x}^{4}+{e}^{3x}\\cdot 4{x}^{3}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡{x}^{4} \\\\  & =3{e}^{3x}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡{x}^{4}+4{x}^{3}{e}^{3x}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡{x}^{4} \\\\  & ={e}^{3x}(3\\operatorname{sinh}⁡{x}^{4}+4{x}^{3}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡{x}^{4})\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514471 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186514311 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514471 #edb/ref 1069 "q-95326" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514471 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514471 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\nFind the derivative of $t(x)=\\frac{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x}{{e}^{x}}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514471 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e582897a-43fa-53c9-83f2-0eb49fceb2e4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514471 #edb/ref 1074 "In this case, the expression for $t(x)$ is a quotient $\\frac{u(x)}{v(x)}$ with $u(x)=\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x$ and $v(x)={e}^{x}.$ \n\nTherefore, we apply the quotient rule as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{t}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{{u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x)^{′}\\cdot {e}^{x}-\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x\\cdot ({e}^{x})^{′}}{({e}^{x})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x-{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x}{{e}^{2x}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{x}(\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x-\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x)}{{e}^{2x}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x-\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x}{{e}^{x}}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514477 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186514268 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514477 #edb/ref 1069 "q-95683" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514477 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514477 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\nFind the derivative of $f(x)=\\frac{2}{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514477 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f4f3ca36-fa30-5fa4-b1a8-a0cc296aaddc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514477 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we express $f(x)$ as a composite function:\n\n$$\nf=\\frac{2}{g},\\,g=\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x\n$$\n\nThe chain rule states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}g}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}g}=-\\frac{2}{{g}^{2}},\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x,\n$$\n\nFinally, multiplying the two results together and substituting for $g$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{2}{{g}^{2}}\\cdot \\operatorname{sinh}⁡x \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{{cosh}^{2}⁡x}\\cdot \\operatorname{sinh}⁡x \\\\  & =-\\frac{2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x}{{cosh}^{2}⁡x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514478 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186514213 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514478 #edb/ref 1069 "q-95321" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514478 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514478 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\nFind the derivative of $t(x)=\\frac{\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x}{x}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514478 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f50f96cb-b22b-5bd9-91c4-b27ea7e844e6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186514478 #edb/ref 1074 "In this case, the expression for $t(x)$ is a quotient $\\frac{u(x)}{v(x)}$ with $u(x)=\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x$ and $v(x)=x.$ \n\nTherefore, we apply the quotient rule as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{t}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{{u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x)^{′}\\cdot x-\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x\\cdot (x)^{′}}{(x)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{x\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x-\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x}{{x}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
